KNOWNBUG: [except.ctor]/1-3 -- the exceptional edge at a call site runs no
destructors, so objects constructed between try entry and a throwing call (g1)
and locals of intermediate functions without a try (g2) are never destroyed
(assertion currently FAILS).  Level-by-level unwinding between try levels is
fixed; this remaining gap needs guarded call-site unwind blocks emitted by the
goto conversion.  Flip to CORE once call-site unwinding runs these destructors.
